## Round 1 evidence checkpoint (scientific review accepted)

Frozen brief committed before search: 6eead17a. Report and matrices:
`docs/jetp-audits/0735/report.md`, `landmark-coverage.csv`,
`operation-coverage.csv`, `acquisition-log.csv`, `archive-manifest.json`,
`local-input-manifest.json` in the same directory.

20/20 acquisition units; no expansion. June 2010 and June 2020 original rosters
support listed membership, including unfinished projects; June 2015 remains
unlocated and June 2021 inaccessible. Three HTTP archives failed DNS: no original
byte hashes invented. Existing local discovery inputs are hashed. Dates and
missing endpoints are explicit; zero original approval/signature pairs.

The 2010 roster removes entries after signing OR withdrawal. That rule is not
verified for 2020; listed presence cannot prove pending-signature state. Current
snapshot status is separate from historical membership. Triad retained as
unverified protocol candidates; no causal design selected. Ticket stays open
until PR acceptance; underlying archive, frame and endpoint gaps remain visible.

## Independent review

All five documentary exit criteria are addressed as a bounded evidence audit;
this does not establish a usable causal design or complete historical population.
An independent scientific reviewer accepted the report and matrices. Fast gate:
1549 passed, ten skipped; adherence:330 passed, thirteen skipped. The report
records the missing-DVC environment failure and successful hydrated rerun.
Ticket remains open until the report PR is accepted.

## Author-directed second pass, 14 September 2026

The author requests broader coverage beyond World Bank, energy and JETP
countries. Execute the frozen round-2 brief at
`docs/jetp-audits/0735/round2/brief.md`: ADB, AfDB, EIB and AFD routes,
all-sector catalogues and multiple non-JETP borrower strata. This replaces
the first round's single-lender restriction for the new pass only.

Additional acceptance: institution-by-stage availability matrix; documented
non-energy/non-JETP examples; actual milestone pairs where available; explicit
historical-population and dropped/cancelled coverage; costed next acquisition
priorities. Sparse findings remain valid, but narrow WB results are not taken
as evidence about the wider source landscape. No design is selected.
